<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Weapon accuracy (spread) rebalance, applied by ModAdjusterV2 (workshop 3017795356) as field-level patches.
    No SBC definitions are overridden.

    RATIONALE
    1. One spread per caliber. Fixed guns, large-grid turrets and small-grid turrets of the same caliber all share
       the same spread, for simplicity. Small-grid turrets are still balanced by their shorter range (75% of large).
    2. Realistic ordering. Real guns get MORE accurate as they get bigger and slower-firing on stable mounts, so:
       artillery > assault cannon = autocannon > gatling. Vanilla had this partly backwards: the artillery turret
       (0.3 deg) was as loose as a GAU-8, and the assault cannon turret (0.35 / 0.5 deg) was looser than the autocannon.
    3. Not fully realistic on purpose. Real big guns are 5-10x tighter still; at that accuracy artillery would one-shot
       fighters from 3 km. Instead, each gun's miss radius at its max range (see Ranges.xml) lands at roughly 5-8 m:
       large ships are reliably hit at max range, small ships only some of the time, so small ships stay viable.
    4. The gatling is the loosest gun on purpose: rapid-fire point defense works by spreading rounds into a cloud
       (real GAU-8 is ~0.29 deg). This also tempers how hard the point-defense changes hit small fighters.

    Spread values are in degrees (max deviation from the aim line). DeviateShotAngleAiming is kept equal.

    Caliber          Vanilla fixed / L turret / S turret     New (all)   Miss radius at max range
    ===============  ======================================  ==========  ===============================
    Gatling          0.15 / 0.225 / 0.225                    0.25        5.2 m @ 1,200 (S turret 3.9 m @ 900)
    Autocannon       0.15 / 0.25 (Overhaul) / 0.25           0.2         5.6 m @ 1,600 (S turret 4.2 m @ 1,200)
    Assault cannon   0.2 (S fixed) / 0.35 / 0.5              0.2         7.0 m @ 2,000 (S turret 5.2 m @ 1,500)
    Artillery        0.15 (L fixed) / 0.3                    0.15        7.9 m @ 3,000

    Unchanged: rockets (0.5, unguided area weapon), anti-personnel turret (0.15), railguns (0).
    JS - Weapon Overhaul's LargeAutocannonTurret weapon is patched by Data\Scripts\JS - Weapon Rebalance\OptionalModWeaponTuning.cs
    instead, because ModAdjusterV2 throws KeyNotFoundException on missing WeaponDefinitions when Overhaul is not loaded.
-->
<Definitions xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
    xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
    <Weapons>
        <!-- ===== Gatling: 0.25 ===== -->
        <!-- Fixed small-grid gatling gun (vanilla definition) -->
        <Weapon>
            <Id>
                <TypeId>WeaponDefinition</TypeId>
                <SubtypeId>GatlingGun</SubtypeId>
            </Id>
            <DeviateShotAngle>0.25</DeviateShotAngle>
            <DeviateShotAngleAiming>0.25</DeviateShotAngleAiming>
        </Weapon>
        <!-- Fixed small-grid gatling gun (Warfare 2 variant, also used by JS - Weapon Overhaul's SmallGatlingGun) -->
        <Weapon>
            <Id>
                <TypeId>WeaponDefinition</TypeId>
                <SubtypeId>GatlingGunWarfare</SubtypeId>
            </Id>
            <DeviateShotAngle>0.25</DeviateShotAngle>
            <DeviateShotAngleAiming>0.25</DeviateShotAngleAiming>
        </Weapon>
        <!-- Large-grid gatling turret (also the Contact Pack reskin) -->
        <Weapon>
            <Id>
                <TypeId>WeaponDefinition</TypeId>
                <SubtypeId>LargeGatlingTurret</SubtypeId>
            </Id>
            <DeviateShotAngle>0.25</DeviateShotAngle>
            <DeviateShotAngleAiming>0.25</DeviateShotAngleAiming>
        </Weapon>
        <!-- Small-grid gatling turret (also the Contact Pack reskin) -->
        <Weapon>
            <Id>
                <TypeId>WeaponDefinition</TypeId>
                <SubtypeId>SmallGatlingTurret</SubtypeId>
            </Id>
            <DeviateShotAngle>0.25</DeviateShotAngle>
            <DeviateShotAngleAiming>0.25</DeviateShotAngleAiming>
        </Weapon>

        <!-- ===== Autocannon: 0.2 ===== -->
        <!-- Fixed small-grid autocannon -->
        <Weapon>
            <Id>
                <TypeId>WeaponDefinition</TypeId>
                <SubtypeId>Autocannon</SubtypeId>
            </Id>
            <DeviateShotAngle>0.2</DeviateShotAngle>
            <DeviateShotAngleAiming>0.2</DeviateShotAngleAiming>
        </Weapon>
        <!-- Small-grid autocannon turret (also the Warfare 3 Type II) -->
        <Weapon>
            <Id>
                <TypeId>WeaponDefinition</TypeId>
                <SubtypeId>AutocannonTurret</SubtypeId>
            </Id>
            <DeviateShotAngle>0.2</DeviateShotAngle>
            <DeviateShotAngleAiming>0.2</DeviateShotAngleAiming>
        </Weapon>

        <!-- ===== Assault cannon: 0.2 ===== -->
        <!-- Large-grid assault cannon turret (also the Warfare 3 Type II) -->
        <Weapon>
            <Id>
                <TypeId>WeaponDefinition</TypeId>
                <SubtypeId>MediumCalibreTurret</SubtypeId>
            </Id>
